    <info html="&lt;h4 class=&quot;obj-title style-1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#0f5f96; font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;More Terrain Coming Soon &amp; 6 cm of New Snow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Great news. Additional terrain is coming very soon&lt;/strong&gt;, with our crews continuing snowmaking and trail preparation. We also picked up &lt;strong&gt;6 cm of snow yesterday afternoon&lt;/strong&gt;, adding to our early-season base. There’s the possibility of more snow later this week, giving us another reason to look forward to the days ahead.&lt;/p&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Today, enjoy about &lt;strong&gt;2,400 vertical feet of skiing and riding&lt;/strong&gt; from the top of &lt;strong&gt;Grizzly Gondola&lt;/strong&gt; back to the base via Deer Run and Lower Flight. All routes from the gondola start on blue (intermediate) terrain, with Deer Run temporarily rated blue. &lt;strong&gt;Glacier Chair, Juniper Chair and the Magic Carpet&lt;/strong&gt; round out today’s lineup, with &lt;strong&gt;4 lifts, 6 runs and 2 small terrain parks open&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Please ski and ride with care, stay aware of those around you and have a great day on the slopes.&lt;/p&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Save big with early-season lift tickets, &lt;a style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot; href=&quot;https://passes.skilouise.com/en/catalogue/categories/winter-lift-tickets_265/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;available online&lt;/a&gt; and at the resort. Winter lift hours are 9:30 am to 4:30 pm daily. &lt;a style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.skilouise.com/things-to-do/new-lift-hours-for-winter/&quot; &gt;Details here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"/>
