    <comment name="Conditions">More Terrain Coming Soon &amp; 6 cm of New Snow&#13;
Great news. Additional terrain is coming very soon, with our crews continuing snowmaking and trail preparation. We also picked up 6 cm of snow yesterday afternoon, adding to our early-season base. There’s the possibility of more snow later this week, giving us another reason to look forward to the days ahead.&#13;
Today, enjoy about 2,400 vertical feet of skiing and riding from the top of Grizzly Gondola back to the base via Deer Run and Lower Flight. All routes from the gondola start on blue (intermediate) terrain, with Deer Run temporarily rated blue. Glacier Chair, Juniper Chair and the Magic Carpet round out today’s lineup, with 4 lifts, 6 runs and 2 small terrain parks open.&#13;
Please ski and ride with care, stay aware of those around you and have a great day on the slopes.&#13;
Save big with early-season lift tickets, available online and at the resort. Winter lift hours are 9:30 am to 4:30 pm daily. Details here.</comment>
